Insertion Sort:
Insertion Sort takes one element at a time and inserts it into its correct position in the already sorted portion.

Case      	    Time Complexity
Best Case          	O(n)
Average Case	    O(n²)
Worst Case        	O(n²)
Space Complexity	  O(1)

Best case occurs when the array is already sorted.
Worst case occurs when the array is in reverse order.
It works very well for small or nearly sorted datasets.
